{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You</b> — I have already mentioned that it is the practice of the Hebrews to elide the bet, like 'I found the house of YHWH,' and similarly: <b>by Your hand</b> — by Your strength or by Your blow." "The mem [of] ותטעם — return to our fathers." "The lamed [of] לאומים — serves like 'all the לאומים praise Him' [i.e., like לאומים elsewhere where it functions as a gentilic]." "The mem [of] ותשלחם — return to them, like ותגרשם."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:40.779645367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}